Defect 1 & 2: assertNoForgeSecretMaterial was scanning the whole
REST claim 201 body (which must legitimately carry body.token).
Replaced with assertClaimRevealToken(body, forgeToken) — asserts
body.token === forgeToken and scans only body.task / body.lease /
body.clone for leaks — in:
  - 'REST claim without request_id stays 201 and the lease
     envelope is exactly { claim_id, expires_at, ttl_seconds }'
  - 'a single replay reuses the same claim_id and token, and
     audits the re-reveal as a replay without leaking the token'
Audited every other assertNoForgeSecretMaterial call site: the
remaining ones (intruder/conflict/second responses, and the
token-containment test's restList/restDetail/progressed/released)
all scan non-201 or non-claim bodies and were already correct —
left unchanged.

Defect 3: the four-non-terminal-statuses retention test reused one
credential-profile identity across all four loop iterations,
colliding with credential_profiles' UNIQUE (forge, base_url,
repo_full_name) once the first iteration's delete was (correctly)
refused. Gave each status its own profile identity
(repo_full_name suffixed by NON_TERMINAL_STATUS_SLUG[status]) and
matched the referencing task's repo.full_name to it (publish
enforces PROFILE_REPO_MISMATCH_MESSAGE otherwise). Assertion
content (refused for 待认领/进行中/待验收/已退回, allowed for
已完成/已取消) unchanged.
